# Forbidden characters

Never write these two characters anywhere in text you create or edit:

- em dash (Unicode 2014)
- semicolon (Unicode 003B)

This covers UI copy, SEO title and description, Open Graph, Twitter, FAQ, database string values, comments, logs, commit messages, and chat replies.

Use a hyphen, comma, period, or a new sentence instead.

Do not add these characters when changing existing files. If you must keep language syntax that already requires a semicolon (SQL statement end, C++), do not introduce extra ones in strings or comments.

TypeScript and JavaScript you write must not use a semicolon.
